{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed","id":1511173,"title":"Antediluvian Destroyed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-09T19:55:53-07:00","id":1511173,"title":"Antediluvian Destroyed","content":"Have you ever had an Antediluvian destroyed by another character in one of your games? How has it affected the rest of the clan or the game as a whole?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T20:54:51-07:00","id":1511177,"title":"","content":"I played in an elder game for 5+ irl years and the underlying premise was that Gehenna was ensuing, so, yes, some Antediluvians died, and some in ways the coterie took a direct hand in through various shenanigans.<br /> <br /> But, I mean, it was the End Times, that sort of thing comes with the package. It's difficult to pick out a distinct sort of effect thereby when the world is slowly to moderately to quickly (depending on the particular chunk of the world or society) going from pre to actual apocalypse in stages. But I did enjoy when the STs (there were several that traded off) went with the Tzimisce post 1) finding out for legit confirmed realsies they had not killed their founder at all, clan wide, 2) Not even really playing a role in what actually then later killed their founder for legit confirmed realsies 3) Having a huge identity crisis about 1 and 2, ended up in an extended chain of events that lead to them joining the Camarilla, who were facing the disintegrating global situation with an increasing &quot;we will take anyone that is not outright infernal just for the added strength&quot; perspective. It came off in a way that felt like it made sense as far as the way things were played, and why wouldn't they have a huge identity crisis about that combination of events? If anything would make a clan look at their sect and their place in it and go &quot;what was even the point of us&quot;, y'know.<br /> <br /> No one had a Tzimisce pc, before anyone notes &quot;man that would have sucked as an experience for a Tzimisce pc! Just humiliating stuff!&quot; With that said, there were two Assamite pcs, one of whom entirely believed in their clan's core mythos as an in character thing, and Haqim still turned out to be The Worst. We all rolled with the notion that stuff was going to get severely turned on its head and the center cannot hold and what all have you.<br /> <br /> Hey, the Tzim were able to negotiate a justicar out of it, they were fine, relative to the world increasingly crumbling (the Camarilla were not un-desperate).<br /> <br /> (The Sabbat were fine relative to one of their founding boasts being revealed as a big ol nope, it was counterbalanced by &quot;see! we were right!&quot; as far as them there blood gods in fact existing and mostly coming off as everything you never wanted to exist. They picked up a bunch more of the Assamites post a slightly pre revised Clanbook schism that ended up in the Camarilla getting none of them)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 05-10-2023, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T21:09:11-07:00","id":1511179,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I can't think of that being remotely possible, especially since one of them can withstand a neutron bomb, a fucking neutron bomb, unless they diablerize him while he's in tupor. I can think more of trying to survive an event caused by them or stopping one of their plans that they aren't directly involved in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T21:58:57-07:00","id":1511182,"title":"","content":"No, but as I run I tend to have it canon several are dead and I've made it clear they're Killable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T22:29:19-07:00","id":1511185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed?p=1511182#post1511182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, but as I run I tend to have it canon several are dead and I've made it clear they're Killable.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you don't usually use things like the <i>Week of Nightmares</i> and other side effects for the clan as a whole?<br /> To be honest I never liked the idea behind the <i>Week of Nightmares</i> very much, I remember at the time there were people jokingly saying that it was &quot;the way Justin Achillis found to basically 'delete' the clan he said he didn't like&quot; lol<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly, I can't think of that being remotely possible </div> </div> </div>Actually, it's just as possible as the ST wants it to be. My question is more aimed at STs in general as it's harder to find PCs who would ever be able to have a hand in such things, unless we're running a Gehenna scenario. Just as a sidenote, there are Mages and Cainites who are able to create destructive forces similar in power to a nuclear explosion, so it's not that hard to imagine a scenario where one NPC is able to successfully attack and destroy an Antediluvian. As I said before, it all depends on what the ST wants for his story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the underlying premise was that Gehenna was ensuing </div> </div> </div>I see, but then it was more of a Gehenna scenario, right? I've run one such scenario about 15 years ago. Likewise, I was more curious regarding the destruction of a single Antediluvian in an ongoing chronicle and its effects than with an &quot;apocalyptic scenario&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T22:31:25-07:00","id":1511186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed?p=1511182#post1511182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, but as I run I tend to have it canon several are dead and I've made it clear they're Killable.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you don't usually use things like the <i>Week of Nightmares</i> and other side effects for the clan as a whole?<br /> To be honest I never liked the idea behind the <i>Week of Nightmares</i> very much, I remember at the time there were people jokingly saying that it was &quot;the way Justin Achillis found to basically 'delete' the clan he said he didn't like&quot; lol<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly, I can't think of that being remotely possible </div> </div> </div>Actually, it's just as possible as the ST wants it to be. My question is more aimed at STs in general as it's harder to find PCs who would ever be able to have a hand in such things, unless we're running a Gehenna scenario. Just as a sidenote, there are Mages and Cainites who are able to create destructive forces similar in power to a nuclear explosion, so it's not that hard to imagine a scenario where one NPC is able to successfully attack and destroy an Antediluvian. As I said before, it all depends on what the ST wants for his story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the underlying premise was that Gehenna was ensuing </div> </div> </div>I see, but then it was more of a Gehenna scenario, right? I've run one such scenario about 15 years ago. Likewise, I was more curious regarding the destruction of a single Antediluvian in an ongoing chronicle and its effects than with an &quot;apocalyptic scenario&quot;\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T22:37:19-07:00","id":1511188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed?p=1511182#post1511182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, but as I run I tend to have it canon several are dead and I've made it clear they're Killable.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you don't usually use things like the <i>Week of Nightmares</i> and other side effects for the clan as a whole?<br /> To be honest I never liked the idea behind the <i>Week of Nightmares</i> very much, I remember at the time there were people jokingly saying that it was &quot;the way Justin Achillis found to basically 'delete' the clan he said he didn't like&quot; lol<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly, I can't think of that being remotely possible </div> </div> </div>Actually, it's just as possible as the ST wants it to be. My question is more aimed at STs in general as it's harder to find PCs who would ever be able to have a hand in such things, unless we're running a Gehenna scenario. Just as a sidenote, there are Mages and Cainites who are able to create destructive forces similar in power to a nuclear explosion, so it's not that hard to imagine a scenario where one NPC is able to successfully attack and destroy an Antediluvian. As I said before, it all depends on what the ST wants for his story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the underlying premise was that Gehenna was ensuing </div> </div> </div>I see, but then it was more of a Gehenna scenario, right? I've run one such scenario about 15 years ago. Likewise, I was more curious regarding the destruction of a single Antediluvian in an ongoing chronicle and its effects than with an &quot;apocalyptic scenario&quot;\u200b.<br /> <br /> I know it's not an everyday occurrence, but I'm curious to hear if and how you guys have experienced such scenarios.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T23:02:51-07:00","id":1511189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed?p=1511188#post1511188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, you don't usually use things like the <i>Week of Nightmares</i> and other side effects for the clan as a whole?<br /> To be honest I never liked the idea behind the <i>Week of Nightmares</i> very much, I remember at the time there were people jokingly saying that it was &quot;the way Justin Achillis found to basically 'delete' the clan he said he didn't like&quot; lol<br /> <br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its contextually dependant, ravnos was one of objectively more powerful members of the 3rd and was proactively harming his clan. With the ravnos I've made a point they're effectively a Sabbat clan now due to most survivors being in that faction and Liberal embracing policies.<br /> <br /> By contrast I also run lasombra as dead but since its death was a botched attempt at apotheosis by obtenerbration it didn't really harm the clan.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T23:13:17-07:00","id":1511190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed?p=1511188#post1511188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I see, but then it was more of a Gehenna scenario, right? I've run one such scenario about 15 years ago. Likewise, I was more curious regarding the destruction of a single Antediluvian in an ongoing chronicle and its effects than with an &quot;apocalyptic scenario&quot;\u200b.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It was, but for being a long term campaign, it wasn't everything exploding within a very narrow time frame, if you follow (I mean things were exploding, but across several years of in game time as well). There were peaks and valleys and some events had more time to have the fallout of them rain down on people. It was just, nothing happened in isolation, if that makes sense.<br /> <br /> But yeah, not quite what you're looking for then.<br /> <br /> I would say even though it's in no way anything like what the writers had some overarching idea for, I do find it interesting in canon that some antediluvian deaths mattered spectacularly (Ravnos, as noted), whereas others, if you went with they were dead, amounted to a footnote (Ventrue for instance). It's completely accidental that a vibe results from that being the case, but it's a vibe that I like. *Maybe* the god dying breaks everything, and *maybe* it barely matters for anything, and there's no way to know until it happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T23:35:57-07:00","id":1511192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed?p=1511189#post1511189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Its contextually dependant, ravnos was one of objectively more powerful members of the 3rd and was proactively harming his clan. With the ravnos I've made a point they're effectively a Sabbat clan now due to most survivors being in that faction and Liberal embracing policies.<br /> <br /> By contrast I also run lasombra as dead but since its death was a botched attempt at apotheosis by obtenerbration it didn't really harm the clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. Poor Lasombra, I remember I made a point of &quot;making him justice&quot; one day, because I've always felt the developers of the setting had a falling for the Tzimisce Antediluvian. Since the first time I read about the diablerie of the two, it's rather easy to read in between the lines that Tzimisce obviously survived Lugoj's attack, etc, while with Lasombra it's like &quot;nobody cares&quot; hahaha, not to mention the presence of the &quot;Eldest&quot; is much more felt in the setting. I swear that if I proceed with this plan of a &quot;Gehenna like scenario&quot;, I'll make Tzimisce the first Antediluvian to fall hahaha...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But yeah, not quite what you're looking for then. </div> </div> </div>Quite the opposite, I'd say. If it was a long story and not a short &quot;Gehenna scenario&quot;, as you mentioned I'm interested. I just don't plan to make things happpen &quot;too fast&quot; like in the Gehenna scenarios from <i>Time of Judgment</i>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T23:53:00-07:00","id":1511193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed?p=1511192#post1511192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting. Poor Lasombra, I remember I made a point of &quot;making him justice&quot; one day, because I've always felt the developers of the setting had a falling for the Tzimisce Antediluvian. Since the first time I read about the diablerie of the two, it's rather easy to read in between the lines that Tzimisce obviously survived Lugoj's attack, etc, while with Lasombra it's like &quot;nobody cares&quot; hahaha, not to mention the presence of the &quot;Eldest&quot; is much more felt in the setting. I swear that if I proceed with this plan of a &quot;Gehenna like scenario&quot;, I'll make Tzimisce the first Antediluvian to fall hahaha...<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I decided that one the Sabbat ones should die to emphasise that it's a meaningful conflict. Tzmisce I tend to write weakened after Samuel killed it. Its cheated death by vissitude but its less than it was intellectually and power wise.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T00:12:12-07:00","id":1511194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tzmisce I tend to write weakened after Samuel killed it. Its cheated death by vissitude but its less than it was intellectually and power wise. </div> </div> </div>That's a very good point, actually. The setting sometimes seems to &quot;forget&quot; that Samiel has already killed it once, or at the very least driven it to torpor, I don't remember if the text is clear about it, it's been a while since I've read the Salubri Clanbook (if I'm not mistaken the accounts of Samiel's crusade is in there, right? It's been quite a while since I don't read about it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T15:28:11-07:00","id":1511292,"title":"","content":"I have the 1st - 5th Gens all destroyed in Anno Domini.<br /> <br /> This takes care of most of the &quot;WTF?&quot; powers. The 6th generation is also the largest at this point in time, so each clan stays quite strong in the elders department without sleeping blood gods using them as pawns.<br /> <br /> The Tremere never come about, however the Giovanni are a blood line offshoot of the Cappadocians with Augustus lowering his generation to 6th through diablerie.<br /> <br /> I use most of first edition and a good chunk of second edition as even though I used the V20 and DAV20 for awhile I decided early second edition is when the game peaked. Mages use Thaumaturgy+ various other powers books (Sorcery, numina, Etc...) without blood requirements, Mummy are unchanged, Werewolves use the vampire game version, Ghosts have some Thaumaturgy paths.<br /> <br /> I love Chicago by night so much I just change the generations of a bunch of them. Having lived there for 40+ years it's the city I understand and know the best and have no problems setting a game there from another state.<br /> <br /> I doubt anyone is going to follow my lead here, but as a story teller I killed them all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T16:58:44-07:00","id":1511304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I doubt anyone is going to follow my lead here, but as a story teller I killed them all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b </div> </div> </div>It's at the same time related to the topic being discussed and at the same time it's not, because it seems your story differs a lot from the &quot;standard&quot; game (whatever that means lol), but I'd still be interested in knowing how it all came about, as I stated in the thread, I'm interested in hearing stories where this kind of thing happened. In this way &quot;how&quot; is more important to me, so, using a word you used &quot;WTF&quot; happened in your story? Did the destruction of the Antediluvians affect the rest of the Cainite society, if so, how?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T21:47:05-07:00","id":1511327,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12348_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12348\" data-vbnamecard=\"12348\">Herr Meister</a><br /> <br /> Basically the lowest generations are destroyed with the birth of Christ the most powerful and least human of the Cainites are reduced to ash in that moment, including Caine himself. There isn't a week of nightmares or any other ramifications to the weaker generations.<br /> <br /> The biggest change for vampire society is that it's most powerful members are basically free of Blood Bonds and the like all at the same instant. This leads to the Inconnu forming within a decade made up of some of the eldest 6th generation vampires and some of their 7th generation Childer. I have the Camarilla forming sooner for safety against a more powerful church/or less powerful vampire society depending on how you want to look at it, and the Sabbat forms at the same time, basically just a split on views of how vampire society should be ruled. Both sects are manipulated by the Inconnu, I don't have a tal'mahe'ra without the Antediluvians, just a black hand for the Sabbats special forces.<br /> <br /> The biggest change is to the modern times. While in normal VTM the Antediluvians helped human advancement by pushing science and reason to combat the power of the church (in my game), without them the churches hold is much stronger. Christianity never declines and instead continues to grow, while technology is slowed in some areas and never discovered in others.<br /> <br /> It lets me have modern technology that I think is important for a modern game (printing press, cars, guns, finger printing, telephone, antibiotics) while removing all the things I think ruin VTM. In my world WW1 never happens. Without WW1 the circumstances that allow Hitler to rise to power do not exist so no WW2. Because of this medical advances drop dramatically, modern warfare isn't perfected, plane travel advances are slowed, as well as things like canned goods, and most importantly we never invent the computer.<br /> <br /> So while you have film, radio, primitive analog car phones, you lose Satellites, GPS, space travel, digital clocks phones and cameras. World population is lower without some key medical and agricultural advances, the world is a much bigger place without the internet and easy instant communication/information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T22:43:45-07:00","id":1511329,"title":"","content":"Wasn't it easier for the world to stop only in the nineties and first half of the 2000s?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T12:52:05-07:00","id":1511398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed?p=1511327#post1511327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12348_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12348\" data-vbnamecard=\"12348\">Herr Meister</a><br /> <br /> Basically the lowest generations are destroyed with the birth of Christ the most powerful and least human of the Cainites are reduced to ash in that moment, including Caine himself. There isn't a week of nightmares or any other ramifications to the weaker generations.<br /> <br /> The biggest change for vampire society is that it's most powerful members are basically free of Blood Bonds and the like all at the same instant. This leads to the Inconnu forming within a decade made up of some of the eldest 6th generation vampires and some of their 7th generation Childer. I have the Camarilla forming sooner for safety against a more powerful church/or less powerful vampire society depending on how you want to look at it, and the Sabbat forms at the same time, basically just a split on views of how vampire society should be ruled. Both sects are manipulated by the Inconnu, I don't have a tal'mahe'ra without the Antediluvians, just a black hand for the Sabbats special forces.<br /> <br /> The biggest change is to the modern times. While in normal VTM the Antediluvians helped human advancement by pushing science and reason to combat the power of the church (in my game), without them the churches hold is much stronger. Christianity never declines and instead continues to grow, while technology is slowed in some areas and never discovered in others.<br /> <br /> It lets me have modern technology that I think is important for a modern game (printing press, cars, guns, finger printing, telephone, antibiotics) while removing all the things I think ruin VTM. In my world WW1 never happens. Without WW1 the circumstances that allow Hitler to rise to power do not exist so no WW2. Because of this medical advances drop dramatically, modern warfare isn't perfected, plane travel advances are slowed, as well as things like canned goods, and most importantly we never invent the computer.<br /> <br /> So while you have film, radio, primitive analog car phones, you lose Satellites, GPS, space travel, digital clocks phones and cameras. World population is lower without some key medical and agricultural advances, the world is a much bigger place without the internet and easy instant communication/information.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, that's a very &quot;wild and crazy&quot; scenario, very different from our ordinary experience in the setting.<br /> Anyway thanks for telling me the story. It's interesting to play with alt history settings, I remember about 20+ years ago I ST a scenario where the Axis had won the Second World War and they divided the world between them, it was a very wild story and I was very young, it was also a short story (fortunately lol).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T13:34:21-07:00","id":1511400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed?p=1511329#post1511329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't it easier for the world to stop only in the nineties and first half of the 2000s?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh for sure, the game started in the past and I needed to drop the Tremere for example. The modern world just felt the ramifications, I just liked it. I always change lots of stuff though.<br /> <br /> One last thing and I'll stop the derailment, tech would need to stop advancing before 2000 for me to feel the technology level was right for VTM. Internet and cellphone use was way too prevalent in 2000. 98 was when pretty much everyone had a computer and was online (I'd guess 40% of homes in the US), most got rid of dial up around 98 as well and things just went into hyperdrive. 93-94 (Pre windows 95 with Sslloooww internet speeds that kept you from using video or even pictures and heavy graphics) would probably work out and would be the latest I would go technology wise in a modern VTM game.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12348_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12348\" data-vbnamecard=\"12348\">Herr Meister</a><br /> <br /> Np, glad you enjoyed it. Sounds like I would have enjoyed your game!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T13:51:03-07:00","id":1511402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed?p=1511400#post1511400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh for sure, the game started in the past and I needed to drop the Tremere for example. The modern world just felt the ramifications, I just liked it. I always change lots of stuff though.<br /> <br /> One last thing and I'll stop the derailment, tech would need to stop advancing before 2000 for me to feel the technology level was right for VTM. Internet and cellphone use was way too prevalent in 2000. 98 was when pretty much everyone had a computer and was online (I'd guess 40% of homes in the US), most got rid of dial up around 98 as well and things just went into hyperdrive. 93-94 (Pre windows 95 with Sslloooww internet speeds that kept you from using video or even pictures and heavy graphics) would probably work out and would be the latest I would go technology wise in a modern VTM game.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My mind got a little bugged there because in my country, until we left dial-up internet it was in 2004 - 2005","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T14:07:56-07:00","id":1511404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed?p=1511402#post1511402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My mind got a little bugged there because in my country, until we left dial-up internet it was in 2004 - 2005</div> </div> </div> </div>If I may ask, where do you live?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Np, glad you enjoyed it. Sounds like I would have enjoyed your game! </div> </div> </div>By the way, talking about &quot;wild and crazy ideas&quot;, sometime ago I had this idea of a mage super villain (something like a Voormas on steroids) who would stop the Order of Reason (the pre-technocrats, as you may all know) and &quot;bring back the Mythic Age&quot;, so that the world would never &quot;advance technologically&quot; past the renaissance and magic would be much easier to cast, with less paradox, etc, while on the other hand, technology would be vulgar and prone to paradox. I haven't touched this project in quite a while, but sometimes I think about it and I told my players and they quite enjoyed, I would just need to think more about it to elaborate well how to implement it without it being silly (hard mission, I know) hahaha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 05-11-2023, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T14:10:35-07:00","id":1511405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed?p=1511404#post1511404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I may ask, where do you live?</div> </div> </div> </div>South America<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T23:02:16-07:00","id":1511428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed?p=1511405#post1511405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> South America</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Given's Brazilian prominent place on the internet nowadays one wouldn't suspect it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T23:56:33-07:00","id":1511430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed#post1511173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you ever had an Antediluvian destroyed by another character in one of your games? How has it affected the rest of the clan or the game as a whole?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends<br /> Usually avoid the Antediluvian's destruction, becasue they are integral part of the looming danger<br /> I mean even the &quot;canon&quot; death is not really... well happened<br /> Cappadocius survived, became a wraith, then a Specter, Augustus Giovanni tried the diablerie, but basically failed, and the True Vessel complicated the matters as a bonus - maybe thats why there are no 4th generation Giovanni around whom Augustus Embraced after the &quot;diablerie&quot;<br /> The Lasombra Antediluvian escaped in to the Abyss and no one can recall basicalyl what happened in the Castel d'Ombro...<br /> The Ventrue Antediluvian despite its death embraced left and right (to be honest I preferred Justin Achilli's comment 20+ years ago, who suggested the Ventrue amcient used Fortitude 10 to wait for Gehenna to be over avoiding the Jhyad and surviving it that way. For all tense and purposes he was dead when used fortitude, but then simply revived himself. When it suited him ,he was dead. When not, walked around doing his stuff.)<br /> Malkav survived as the Maddness Network (After the fall of the Second City, Malkav is believed to have traveled towards the city of Petra. It is along this journey that some think the Eldest Malkavian was attacked and torn asunder. Who the assailant might have been is unknown, though it seems likely that another Antediluvian sought his destruction. Yet even if his body was destroyed, it is believed that his spirit survived inside of his childer, who gathered at the site of his death and drank his spilled blood, taking Malkav's essence into them and sheltering it from the sun's rays)<br /> Tzimsice... well you know the story<br /> The Brujah antediluvian depends, I like the idea, there was no Trolie, the cold and calculating Ilyes devoured his lover/child and the act shattered his mind, and became &quot;Her&quot;, an alternate personality... (and thats the reason why Trolie is sometimes male, sometimes female... and no one punsihed Troile for eating Ilyes... simply becasue it not happened, just a Sire consumed is child) or used Temporis. Dealers choice\u200b<br /> Saulot is a can of worms that requires his own topic...<br /> Zapathasura? Oh boy... the idea the whole frenzy prevented him to use powers is quite silly. Zappy not only had Chimestry, but Animalism, and several of its power basically makes you either immune to Frenzy or allows you too keep your sanity, ride the Wave, or simply toss out your beast (I actually had a funny session where tho' Zappy escaped destruction, his P'o/Beast - was a bitly crossover story with KotE - wandered away, and the party in service of the antediluvian (and other ancients) had to track it down and capture the host tiger, that became a Raksahsa-like demon) out to pester others<br /> Another flaw in that theory, the Week of Nightmares was around most likely Monday, June 28 to Sunday, July 4, 1999. Thats... darn long time for a frenzy! And against the three of the eldest Kuei-jin Bodhisattvas Zappy used a plathora of powers not just brute might, fang and claws...<br /> Thats not really possible if you are out of your mind in a Frenzy And... there is that little V5 thing, called:<br /> &quot;Blood of Zapathasura&quot; - Thick, <b>sentient</b> ropes of his vitae stained the ground in Bangladesh where he fell. The noonday sun <b>did not destroy it all</b>. You own a small vial containing the Blood of the Ravnos Antediluvian. What you do with this vitae is up to you, and what it does to anyone who imbibes it is up to the Storyteller.<br /> Funny to think, Zapathasura became Venom-like Anyhow, Malkav survived destruction after he was torn to shreds, and several of his children gathered and consumed his blood, shileding it from the sun, in themselves... Maybe Zappy pulled a Malkav<br /> <br /> The only Antediluvian I tend to use as &quot;destroyed&quot; is Stuekh.<br /> Well not destroyed but... banished.<br /> Thus, the Followers of Set are not the &quot;true&quot; Children of Sutekh - well, they are - , but Sutekh had been betrayed by one (or more) of his direct childer and has been banished to Duat (maybe Set, who is a seperate vampire and visited the Cainites and at the heart of Arike with Absimiliard)<br /> His Clan, which he originally founded to be a mighty tribe which preached individuality and self-reliance, has instead been corrupted into it's present day form (thanks to Apep/Wyrm nice tie with the Werewolf/Mummy). Thus, the Clan of Faith, the Mesu Bedshet (Chilren of Rebellion) became the Followers of Set.<br /> Except, not all his childer forgot his ideals and a small core of them have been watching and waiting for thousands of years and now their ready to strike back against their corrupted brethern.<br /> Would they have Serpentis or something else, implying that the snake imagery was a later addition? Usually Akhu especially &quot;Weather Control&quot; like the Thaumaturgy path, as Sutekh was god of storms, not to mention they are warriors, since Sutekh was the mighty champion of Ra, so Potence, Akhu, Presence.<br /> Set/sutekh was not affilated with Serpents until a later period in Egyptian history, when he came to be associated with Apep. Before that he was seen as a protector of Ra, who fought Apep.<br /> Before his banishment Sutekh as the ex-champion of Ra, was the one who cursed his rebellious children with their curse of being extremely suceptible to light... in those stories, there are &quot;True Setites&quot; who have a differnt curse altogether, like the True Brujah)<br /> But that is the closest I wandered in to the destroyed Antediluvian territory\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 05-12-2023, 05:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-12T17:40:19-07:00","id":1511491,"title":"","content":"Really nice post concerning many Antediluvians, thank you for your time and effort. I found this to be particularly interesting as it's new information to me:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Ventrue Antediluvian despite its death embraced left and right (to be honest I preferred Justin Achilli's comment 20+ years ago, who suggested the Ventrue amcient used Fortitude 10 to wait for Gehenna to be over avoiding the Jhyad and surviving it that way. For all tense and purposes he was dead when used fortitude, but then simply revived himself. When it suited him ,he was dead. When not, walked around doing his stuff.) </div> </div> </div>Do you know where can I find the source for his statement? I never looked at Fortitude this way and the idea is quite clever and wanted to read it myself. In general I think the problem with Set is that some of the ideas about him and his nature kind of contradic each other and, more importantly, all the established lore of the other sources and the same happened with Haqim many times. Like the ideas that Set was in reality the first vampire or that Haqim was of the second generation, instead of the third, among other things. Then there's this problem that these ideas could only work if you basically disregard everything else in favor of their vision, I've always felt it was problematic. I once had a player who used to love the Assamites and he said that he believed Haqim was of the Second Generation and I basically said it's BS lol The same applies to Set in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-12T23:59:09-07:00","id":1511511,"title":"","content":"It was more than two decades ago ^^<br /> Somewhere on the net I'm sure the interview is <i>somewhere (</i>among others, like how the Week of Nightmares was an overcorrection and the Ravnos weren't killed off because of the past stereotypes, but because Justin Achilli personally hated the Ravnos and he was the head writer of Vampire at the time and had unlimited creative control over the line.<br /> The original plan for the Week of Nightmares was to kill off the Followers of Set since they were the least popular clan among players at the time and the original plan to kill off the Setites was that Set would awaken and summon his whole clan to Egypt and then kill off the clan after a grand judgment.<br /> A modified version of that original scene appears in one of the Gehenna scenarios.) but lead writer or not, it was his &quot;version&quot;, not canon by any mean - everyone know the Ventrue was Justin pet clan and he loved them (still oves them)<br /> But it explain in a nice way, how and way this anomaly with the 1st ed version (Brujah Antediluvian cut of the Ventrue ante's head out the walls of the city, and thats why every vampire accept the ventrue rule, as a remorse/penitent...) and the later Embraces. Justin claimed that he faked his Final Death when he left the Second City and survived Gehenna in the same way with fortitude 10 ; this way making him the last Kindred as well as the only one to have survived God's Wrath...<i>twice</i>.<br /> Not canon mind you, but explain a lot of thing<br /> <br /> As for Haqim, I tend to use the (not really canon) version Published by Justin Achilli, the alternative history of the Assamite clan. It was originally written by Clayton Oliver for inclusion in Clanbook: Assamite Revised. However this chapter didn't make it to the final print. It is undeveloped and unedited, and as such not &quot;official&quot;. Nonetheless it's an interesting read.<br /> From the Assamite.com (now gone site):<br /> <br /> <b>The Martyr-General</b><br /> Many Path of Blood adherents, including ur-Shulgi and the members of the Web of Knives, preach a wholly divergent tale that casts not only the other Antediluvians but Caine and the Second Generation as the villains. According to this story, Haqim was never Embraced; rather, he deliberately made himself into a vampire in order to combat Caine<br /> Thousands of years ago, a great city stood in what the mortals now call the Fertile Crescent. This city's name was En'esh - &quot;Enoch,&quot; to the Cainites. The king of En'esh, a wise and just man, was named Khe-duk. His queen, beautiful and noble, was Liada. As was the city's tradition, the eldest prince had no name but that of his city, En'esh, in order to remind him of the duty to his people for which he was being groomed. And the king's spear and shield, the lord of the armies of En'esh, the most trusted advisor and closest confidant of the royal family, was a man named Haqim.<br /> One night, as Haqim and En'esh were inspecting the guards on duty, a traveler approached the western gates of the city. He hailed the gates, asking the guards to grant him entrance. Despite the law of the city, which required the gates to remain barred through the night as a defense against bandits, the troops opened the gate and allowed the traveler entrance. Haqim was outraged at this gross breach of discipline and would have flown into a rage, but En'esh stayed his hand. &quot;He is one man, alone and unarmed,&quot; the prince said, &quot;and the guards obviously saw this and allowed him entry out of charity. Are we so poor a people that we cannot extend trust to harmless vagabonds? Duty must be tempered with compassion; you yourself taught me that.&quot; Saying so, the prince approached the traveler and bade him introduce himself.<br /> The stranger bowed to the prince. &quot;My name is Khayyin,&quot; he said, &quot;and I have traveled the wastes for weeks in search of the city whose name I heard spoken in distant lands. The greatest city in the world, they called it, and I see that they spoke truth.&quot; He continued in this vein for some minutes, lavishing praises upon the city En'esh and the family of the prince En'esh.<br /> The prince was entranced by this glib-tongued traveler and said to Haqim, &quot;Surely one so wise and courtly as this Khayyin must be a noble in disguise. Perhaps he is an exile, expelled from his homeland by some war or coup - or perhaps he has come to us in this guise to seek alliance with En'esh. We must treat him with the respect that he surely deserves.&quot; Saying this, the prince bowed to Khayyin and bade him stay in the palace during his time in the city.<br /> Haqim said nothing, for it was not his place to question a member of the royal family - at least, not in public. But his eyes were keen, and his ears were sharp, and his instincts were strong, and he saw the secret smile that flickered behind Khayyin's face when the prince issued his invitation.<br /> Before dawn the next morning, Haqim requested a private audience with the king and queen, thinking to alert them to the viper their son had clutched to his heart. But as he entered the throne room, he saw that he had not struck swiftly enough, for seated beside the king, in the place reserved for visiting nobility, was the traveler Khayyin.<br /> Haqim knew better than to speak out against Khayyin then - he was no coward, and feared no man's wrath for insults real or imagined, but he held to propriety. Quickly, he gathered his thoughts and improvised - telling no lie, as his honor required, but only reporting that part of the truth which would not cause conflict. &quot;My liege,&quot; he said to the king, &quot;I see that my audience is unnecessary, for you have already met the man whose entrance to the city I sought to report to you. I came here thinking to forewarn you of the presence of a visiting noble in En'esh, but obviously you have already made his acquaintance. With your leave, I will return to my duties.&quot;<br /> The king nodded and bade Haqim return to his soldiers. But Haqim saw the serpent's smile in Khayyin's eyes again, and he knew that the visitor held no illusions about Haqim's true purpose in requesting audience with the king. Haqim's heart was heavy, for he alone knew the threat that Khayyin held for the city of En'esh. He could not say what the stranger's intentions were, but he knew in his heart that Khayyin would bring ruin upon the city if his plans were left unchecked. That day, he spoke to the palace guards, instructing them to keep close watch on Khayyin. Then he went to the practice field to oversee his soldiers' training.<br /> Days became weeks, and weeks became months, and the season turned from planting time to harvest time, and still Khayyin stayed within the palace. Haqim often saw him in the evenings when the general went to court. Sometimes, he was playing stones with the king and his other advisors; sometimes, reciting poetry to the queen and her ladies; all too often, keeping company with the prince, whispering advice and observations into the young man's ear. And whenever Khayyin saw Haqim, the visitor smiled his hidden smile, as if daring Haqim to strike at him.<br /> The general was unsettled, for he was charged with the defense of the city, yet he was powerless to strike at the single greatest threat to En'esh. His frustration wore on his temper, and his face became lined and gray, and the soldiers whispered that their general was troubled. This troubled them in turn, for they loved their leader in the way that only men who have shared the terror of the battlefield can love, and not a man among them would not have gladly given his life for Haqim. They plotted and schemed, in their own loyal way, and gradually they reached a decision.<br /> One afternoon, as the lord of the armies watched his soldiers casting their spears against targets of straw, a small band of his lieutenants approached him. These were his most trusted subordinates, men who had fought at his side for their entire adult lives, and there were no barriers between them. Their faces were grim, as if they were reporting the collapse of the army's flank on the battlefield, and Haqim dreaded to hear their words - yet he could not turn them away.<br /> &quot;We have noticed,&quot; said one of the soldiers, &quot;that you are not the same man that you were in days of old, when you led us against the tribes and nations that surround the lands of En'esh. Some of the troops think that garrison life disagrees with you, that you fear stagnation and old age and the inactivity of this year's peace. Yet we know you too well, and we know you are as weary as we ourselves are of bloodshed.&quot;<br /> &quot;And we know the true cause of your discontent,&quot; added a second soldier, &quot;for your soul was not darkened thus before this visitor Khayyin replaced you as the most favored advisor of the royal family. Yet you are too noble a man to fall prey to jealousy, so we know you must think that this man intends to do harm to our rulers.&quot;<br /> &quot;And this troubles us, too,&quot; a third soldier put in, &quot;for this Khayyin is a most unusual man. The soldiers who take guard duty in the palace return with strange tales of him - no so much what he has done as what he has not done. We have dozens of tablets full of the guard commanders' reports on Khayyin's movements, and in not one of them was his presence at a single banquet recorded. Nor have any of our soldiers ever reported seeing him during the day. What manner of man is this, that does not eat and does not embrace the life-giving sun?&quot;<br /> Haqim sighed heavily. &quot;You are right. I do not trust Khayyin, for he shows us a face that tells us nothing of the man behind it. He came to this city in the dead of night, with naught but the rags he called clothes, but now he is exalted like a prince. His honeyed words charm all those who hear him speak, for he always seems to know more than he should about what will catch the heart of any man. And I, too, have seen these things of which you tell me. I have spoken to the wise women, and I have consulted the oracles and the seers, and I fear that this Khayyin is no man at all, but a demon sent from the lands to the east to bring ruin on En'esh.&quot;<br /> At this, the soldiers turned pale, for they all knew the stories of the demons of the east, the servants of the strange gods who held sway over men's souls in those dark lands. But Haqim was quick to reassure them. &quot;Take heart,&quot; said he, &quot;for demons can die, too. Do you not remember the tales of demon-slayers, of heroes, of hunters of all the things that would prey upon men? Now we must become hunters, for the sake of our city and our families, and we will stalk our prey in all the dark places it would take as its own. Attend; here is how we shall begin our hunt.&quot;<br /> Haqim and his soldiers conferred all through that day and long into the night, weaving the web in which they would entrap Khayyin. No man of arms of En'esh would approach him without a comrade by his side, and the outlander would never find a pair of soldiers farther away than the nearest corner. Haqim's most trusted troops would dog his every move and sound the alarm at the first sight or sound of foul play. The reason for this scrutiny, should any questions arise, would be the protection of Khayyin - for surely a man who had risen through the court of En'esh as quickly as he must have gained many enemies, and sooner or later one of them must strike at him lest he become too great a threat to their own power.<br /> The next night, Haqim was in his quarters in the palace, examining maps with two of his lieutenants, when one of the soldiers assigned to watch Khayyin burst into the room. Out of breath and shaking with terror, he gasped out that Khayyin was attacking Prince En'esh. Haqim took up his spear and raced toward the prince's chambers, his lieutenants and their troops close at his heels. In a matter of moments, they arrived to find those doors closed and barred, the remaining guard hammering at them with his fists.<br /> The assembled troops seized a nearby statue and prepared to batter down the doors - but as they tensed to strike, the doors swung open to reveal En'esh. &quot;What is this alarm?&quot; the prince cried out. &quot;Why do you seek to invade my private chambers?&quot;<br /> Haqim strode to the forefront of the group and replied, &quot;my prince, the guards reported the sounds of a struggle within, and I feared that some assassin had come upon you. Though all here know of your prowess with spear and bow, duty commanded that we attempt to intervene, lest you be overwhelmed by sheer numbers or struck down from ambush.&quot;<br /> The prince nodded sharply. &quot;You thought aright, but I fear your response were slower than that of my friend Khayyin, who dispatched the attacker nearly before he could draw his blade.&quot; He gestured into his suite. Surely enough, the outlander appeared then, dragging behind him the corpse of a palace servant. He said nothing, merely tossed the body at Haqim's feet and smiled his hidden smile before turning away.<br /> The guards turned away, muttering darkly among themselves. Haqim heard this, but said nothing to quell it, for he could not find it in his heart to reprimand his loyal troops for giving voice to thoughts that he shared. And another thing stayed his tongue, too; for Haqim alone had seen the prince's pallor, the faint, hastily-removed stains of blood upon his clothing, the distant look in the young man's eyes. And a fear coiled within Haqim's breast that the demon Khayyin had made En'esh one of his kind.<br /> Haqim gathered his lieutenants again, in quiet counsel, and told them of his fears. They did not want to believe, at first, but their leader was sure of himself, and they were not ones to question him. They recognized the iron mask his face had become, the mask he only wore on the battlefield when he had taken his enemy's measure, and they knew that the time to strike had come.<br /> Haqim gathered a score of his strongest spears to him and ordered his lieutenants to take the army of En'esh and secure the palace grounds, allowing no man leave nor entry until he returned with the head of Khayyin. They grumbled, for it was not their way to leave their leader to face danger alone, but they obeyed. Then Haqim and his soldiers entered the palace again.<br /> The lord of the armies knew that it would not be enough to simply strike down Khayyin like a dog. The outlander must be exposed for his true self before the court of En'esh. And so Haqim made his way to the throne room - only to find it empty.<br /> Empty, save for King Khe-duk, sitting on his throne - quietly weeping over the limp body of his youngest daughter, cradled in his lap. And then he raised his face and met Haqim's gaze through eyes that streamed tears of blood, and Haqim knew his duty.<br /> The Beast that rode the king's heart reared its head and growled its rage through bared fangs. And then it spoke to Haqim: &quot;There is no place for you here, war-leader. Return to the village in which you were born, forget this city; take up the plow for the spear; and we will be merciful and spare your fleeting life.&quot;<br /> Haqim shook his head. &quot;I swore an oath,&quot; he said, &quot;and I cannot forsake it.&quot;<br /> The king-demon laughed. &quot;If you fear that the gods will turn upon you for breaking your oath, I release you from it.&quot;<br /> &quot;You cannot,&quot; Haqim said, &quot;for my oath is not to you. It is to the city of En'esh - and it is the city that I now protect from what its king has become.&quot; Fast as a striking leopard, he thrust his spear through the king's left eye and shattered his skull like a melon.<br /> With a howl of fury, the creature that had once been Queen Liada leaped at Haqim from behind the thrones, knocking him to the floor. The soldiers rushed forward to rescue their leader, but the combatants struggled so fiercely that they could not use their spears for fear of piercing Haqim. Yet their aid was unneeded; for Haqim gained the upper hand and, drawing his knife, struck the queen's head from her shoulders in a single blow.<br /> &quot;Now,&quot; spoke Haqim, regaining his feet and recovering his spear, &quot;we will deal with the thing that brought this doom to En'esh.&quot; So saying, he led his soldiers to the doors of the prince's chambers. He did not ask for entry this time, but knocked the door from its hinges with a single blow of his heel, leaping into the darkened room before the massive panel had even struck the floor.<br /> A howling, shrieking thing rushed at Haqim, all slavering fangs and naked talons. The general turned and braced his spear, which sank deep into the creature's breast. As the thing fell back, the light from the open door revealed that it had once been Prince En'esh.<br /> Then a staggering blow struck Haqim from behind, and he fell to his knees, dazed. Dimly, he heard the sound of fighting, as if from a great distance. And when he cleared his head and arose, he beheld the rent and scattered bodies of his soldiers, and heard the footsteps of a fleeing man receding down the corridor. The body of En'esh was nowhere to be seen.<br /> Haqim gave chase, for he knew that Khayyin was the one who had struck him down. The din of battle outside the palace told him he must hurry. He raced down the steps and through the carnage that soaked the palace gardens with blood, snatching up a spear and a handful of javelins from his fallen troops. In the distance, he saw the fleeing form of Khayyin with the body of Prince En'esh across his shoulders. Haqim halted and cast his first javelin, taking the demon through the knee, and Khayyin fell.<br /> Before the outlander could stand again, Haqim was on him, striking again and again with his great spear. Yet Khayyin did not die, despite his grievous wounds. With one hand, he cast Haqim aside like a pebble. And then, as the lord of the armies watched in horror, the demon's rage took him and his blood boiled. With a single stamp of his foot, Khayyin shook the ground, and the buildings of En'esh toppled. With a mighty howl, he breathed out a firestorm and scorched the city's fields. He spread his arms wide and drew in breath, and the blood of the people of En'esh flowed into him like a river.<br /> &quot;Enough!&quot; cried out Haqim. &quot;I will end this now!&quot; He rushed at Khayyin, spear raised high to strike at the demon's heart. But Khayyin grasped Haqim by the throat and shook him like a dog.<br /> &quot;Attend and hear, presumptuous creature,&quot; the demon hissed. &quot;I am the scion of a line older than you can imagine. My God cursed me, yet I found older powers than him and made their strength mine. I would have made this city the heart of an empire of the night to last ten thousand years, and your rulers would have lived forever had you not interfered. Yet now your city lies in ruins, for you thought to oppose me. Remember this, in your final moments: you have failed, and I will begin this work again elsewhere, for the strength of a mortal is nothing against that of my blood.&quot; And he sank his fangs into Haqim's throat and drained him of his life's blood. Then Khayyin cast the general into the ruins of the palace and fled into the night, carrying the limp form of Prince En'esh.<br /> Haqim's few surviving soldiers gathered around the broken body of their leader. Haqim still breathed, but his life was ebbing quickly. He beckoned his three remaining lieutenants closer. As they knelt beside him he whispered to them: &quot;I have seen to the heart of the evil that is Khayyin. He and all he would beget are forsaken by the gods, and yet that very fact gives them great power. Blood is their strength, and it is the dark magic of that blood that makes them what they are. I cannot allow Khayyin's vision of his empire of the night to go unchallenged - though the only path I can see to oppose him may result in my own soul being forfeit. Now, bear me to the throne room, that I may request one last boon of my king and queen.&quot;<br /> The soldiers lifted Haqim up and carried him to the throne room, where the bodies of the king and queen lay where they fell. Haqim knelt before them and whispered a blessing upon their souls, for they had been good and just rulers before Khayyin cursed them. Then he opened his wrists with the sharp edges of the king's crown and, as his life flowed away, he lowered his hands to the pool of blood in which he knelt and drank deep of the water of eternal unlife. When Haqim arose and looked upon his soldiers again, he was no longer mortal.<br /> Then Haqim gathered his soldiers and the last citizens of En'esh and led them from the ruins of the city. They traveled into the mountains to the southeast, and it was there that they made their homes. As they traveled, Haqim wrestled with the taint that he had taken into himself, but the strength of his soul was such that the evil of Khayyin, twice removed, was no match for Haqim's will. Eventually, he mastered it and began to learn the power of the Blood. And when he was strong in the Blood, he raised up the fortress Alamut and his people settled in the valleys beneath the Mountain. And then Haqim began to hunt Khayyin and the gods-forsaken brood that the demon created.<br /> In time, Haqim's most loyal lieutenant approached him and asked to be given the Blood, that he might hunt at his lord's side. Haqim studied the man's soul carefully, for he knew well the dangers that lurked in the Blood, but the man's soul was strong. And so the first Child of Haqim strode out from Alamut that night to hunt at the Ancestor's side.<br /> In time, others came to Alamut, and Haqim gave the strongest and most worthy among them the gift and curse of immortality as well. Those whose spirits needed guidance became lesser servants until such time as they gained in strength. And the Children of Haqim learned well how to hunt the Khayyinin, and how to deceive them, and how to drink the Khayyinin's heart's blood in order to gain their power and remove their evil from the world.<br /> <br /> And down through the ages, this is what we have become. Our skins grow black with the accumulated evil we have absorbed from the Khayyinin, but this outward blackening shows that our souls are not poisoned inwardly. We are tripartite now, the marvel of geometry, the least number of legs that can stand alone: viziers, to tend to the mortals; sorcerers, to ward us and our charges from the Khayyinin's masters; and warriors, to strike at the rot that has become too great for them to merely judge and punish selectively.<br /> <br /> The blood of demons flows in our veins, but it is also the blood of the first nobility to walk the Earth, and it is the blood of Haqim. Those latter legacies give us the strength to shrug off the poison of the gods-forsaken. We are the Children of Haqim: his inheritors, his loyal soldiers, his spears and his hunting leopards.<br /> <br /> And we will not fail him.<br /> \u200b<br /> I love this version, and the fact, Haqim &quot;Self-Embrace&quot; is eerily similar to the Baali practice; the Baali usually only Embrace those who are intelligent and driven. Most who are Embraced into Clan Baali had interest in the occult during their mortal lives.<br /> The Embracing ritual of the Baali is one of their most disturbing rituals. A Baali will capture his or her prey and bring him or her to a site he or she has prepared. There will be a large pit, filled with dozens of decomposing bodies. The Baali drains his or her victim to near death and tosses him or her into the pit. In just one of the corpses the Baali hid their blood inside one of the corpses' heart. If the victim manages to find the heart before they die and drink the blood, they are considered worthy of becoming Baali. Ironically, this makes the Baali the only clan that regularly gives their victim the choice of becoming a vampire or choosing to die.<br /> \u200bA Baali is basically the only vampire who <i>decided</i> to become one and <i>had a choice</i><br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 05-13-2023, 03:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T00:51:34-07:00","id":1511517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Someweher on the net I'm sure the interview is <i>somewhere (</i>among others, like how the Week of Nightmares was an overcorrection and the Ravnos weren't killed off because of the past stereotypes, but because Justin Achilli personally hated the Ravnos and he was the head writer of Vampire at the time and had unlimited creative control over the line.<br /> The original plan for the Week of Nightmares was to kill off the Followers of Set since they were the least popular clan among players at the time and the original plan to kill off the Setites was that Set would awaken and summon his whole clan to Egypt and then kill off the clan after a grand judgment.<br /> A modified version of that original scene appears in one of the Gehenna scenarios.) but lead writer or not, it was his &quot;version&quot;, not canon by any mean - everyone know the Ventrue was Justin pet clan and he loved them (still oves them)\u200b </div> </div> </div>I will try to find this interview. You reminded me of something I thought was just hearsay, that Justin Achilli destroyed the Ravnos because he didn't like them. I didn't know for sure if it was confirmed. The fact that he loves the Ventrue might explain a lot of things that happened in Revised and the scenario that led to Gehenna, even though, to be honest, I've always thought he hated the Tremere as well, because of how the clan suddenly lost A LOT of preeminence in the setting in his &quot;reign&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But it explain in a nice way, how and way this anomaly with the 1st ed version (Brujah Antediluvian cut of the Ventrue ante's head out the walls of the city, and thats why every vampire accept the ventrue rule, as a remorse/penitent...) and the later embraces. Justin claimed that he faked his Final Death when he left the Second City and survived Gehenna in the same way tieh fortitude 10 ; this way making him the last Kindred as well as the only one to have survived God's Wrath...<i>twice</i>.<br /> Not canon mind you, but explain a lot of thing\u200b </div> </div> </div>It's an interesting take, and I'd even say it's much more interesting that having Ventrue destroyed from the start (what makes it very complex to explain many of the Ventrue of 4th generation. Also, as a side note, it's cool because it takes into consideration the last discipline in the Ventrue's arsenal that people tie to them. Most of the times people seem to only remember Dominate (first and foremost) and then Presence as the &quot;main weapons in Ventrue's arsenal&quot;. In fact I like to think the Ventrue's as more martially inclined than what the modern setting makes out of them. I don't like much the idea of the clan as purely politicians, but naturally I'm biased as I storyteller <b>Dark Ages</b> games 95% of the times (at the very least, to be sincere, I think the last time I ST a modern setting game was in 2004 or so lol)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Martyr-General</b><br /> Many Path of Blood adherents, including ur-Shulgi and the members of the Web of Knives, preach a wholly divergent tale that casts not only the other Antediluvians but Caine and the Second Generation as the villains. According to this story, Haqim was never Embraced; rather, he deliberately made himself into a vampire in order to combat Caine\u200b (...) </div> </div> </div>It's a cool story, but as I stated before, I think it's way too problematic to portray in a game, because it also goes against everything else, at least it's better than having Haqim as a <b>Second Generation</b> vampire. To be honest, I think I'd never use it in one of my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T12:36:43-07:00","id":1511642,"title":"","content":"That would be a cool story idea to look into and see what kind of changes it would have on the survivors. Though first off all the eldest direct childer suffer final death as a result due to there potent ties with the antidulivean and perhaps most of the grand childer and the rest may find there supernatural abilities becoming unpredictable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T21:59:41-07:00","id":1511692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed?p=1511642#post1511642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be a cool story idea to look into and see what kind of changes it would have on the survivors. Though first off all the eldest direct childer suffer final death as a result due to there potent ties with the antidulivean and perhaps most of the grand childer and the rest may find there supernatural abilities becoming unpredictable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking of something along these lines, but I want to &quot;thread lightly&quot; since one of the PCs is a Tzimisce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T21:42:26-07:00","id":1520079,"title":"","content":"Well, except for the Ravnos, no ante was ever destroyed. Normally they go somewhere else or become something else. Btw, was little after the Cappadocian death that de divine seals started to haywire, isn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T09:12:04-07:00","id":1520118,"title":"","content":"I usually run them as some dead and gone, some sleeping but most are irrelevant as a factor in the unlife of Kindred (Antiquity) and Cainites (Dark Ages).<br /> <br /> Something I do play with is an idea in that the Antediluvian can send urges and impulses to its Clan which explains part of their cultural behavior. Now a Kindred's Beast will have much more felt influence on any vampire but there's constant little subconscious nodges from the Antediluvian to nodge a certain Clan in certain ways. I haven't thought much about how it would work mechanically or if its an RP thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T09:57:14-07:00","id":1520129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed?p=1511692#post1511692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm thinking of something along these lines, but I want to &quot;thread lightly&quot; since one of the PCs is a Tzimisce.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair in regards to the Tzismce we know he isn't truly gone and is essentially Visscuitde at this point and can show it presence in any kindred that is part of it's lineage and you know that the more knowledgeable Tremere fear this notion.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T12:25:47-07:00","id":1520143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrDrika</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed?p=1520079#post1520079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, except for the Ravnos, no ante was ever destroyed. Normally they go somewhere else or become something else. Btw, was little after the Cappadocian death that de divine seals started to haywire, isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think if you want you can even forcefully say that he faked his own death or what woke up wasn't the Ravnos in fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T12:49:02-07:00","id":1520144,"title":"","content":"For my Vampire setting, I don't use the metaplot from the third or fifth editions, so there's no Week of Nightmares but Antediluvians can in fact be killed. It's just really damn hard to do so. Veddharta isn't dead but was the first of the Antediluvians to fall into a deep torpor, which helped fuel the misconception that the Ventrue Antediluvian met Final Death.<br /> <br /> In fact, I'd have it to where you can actually prevent Gehenna by killing an Antediluvian WITHOUT diablerizing them. Problem is, the majority of the folks who'd have both the motive to take down an Antediluvian and the means to do so are in it for the purpose of diablerie.<br /> <br /> Tremere diablerized Saulot and Augustus Giovanni diablerized Cappadocius, and contrary to canon, Giovanni was very thorough in his destruction of Cappadocius, annihilating him completely.<br /> <br /> Saulot's soul was able to survive the Tremere diablerization but he had planned for that. With that said, I'm going with the &quot;unironic Lawful Good heroic saint&quot; depiction of Saulot from early 2e. He foresaw the end and realized he needed to let the Tremere rise to power for both Kindred and Kine to prevent Gehenna or at the very least be able to survive it.<br /> <br /> As for the Baali? If I were to include them in a chronicle, I'm gonna go with the &quot;Always Chaotic Evil&quot; Chick Tract-tier strawman Satanist versions of the Baali from First Edition, but I'm gonna totally rewrite their backstory. Saulot had no hand in their creation but instead it was the work of Sutekh. A failed experiment of Set gone wrong.<br /> <br /> The first Baali was the Methuselah Shaitan, his name a corruption of Set-Han, in fact, Shaitan tried to usurp Set alongside his siblings Moloch and Nergal. They went renegade and consorted with demons to try and gain more power and overthrow Set. Yet the Baali are far more base and crude than the Setites in their quest to spread total corruption.<br /> <br /> But that was long ago and the Baali no longer care for Set nor his Followers while the Setites still hold a deep-seated hatred of the Baali, though most Setite neonates and ancilla believe the Baali to be extinct, if they even know they exist at all. Even many Elders believe the Baali to be a mere historical footnote.<br /> <br /> But the most ancient of Setite elders still know and still remember. They know the Baali are still around and that Set has not forgiven them for their treachery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":".  Fixed a typo 08-08-2023, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T12:51:50-07:00","id":1520145,"title":"","content":"Tried to fix a spelling error and once again, my post got flagged as spam. So forgive me for the double-post.<br /> <br /> For my Vampire setting, I don't use the metaplot from the third or fifth editions, so there's no Week of Nightmares but Antediluvians can in fact be killed. It's just really damn hard to do so. Veddharta isn't dead but was the first of the Antediluvians to fall into a deep torpor, which helped fuel the misconception that the Ventrue Antediluvian met Final Death.<br /> <br /> In fact, I'd have it to where you can actually prevent Gehenna by killing an Antediluvian WITHOUT diablerizing them. Problem is, the majority of the folks who'd have both the motive to take down an Antediluvian and the means to do so are in it for the purpose of diablerie.<br /> <br /> Tremere diablerized Saulot and Augustus Giovanni diablerized Cappadocius, and contrary to canon, Giovanni was very thorough in his destruction of Cappadocius, annihilating him completely.<br /> <br /> Saulot's soul was able to survive the Tremere diablerization but he had planned for that. With that said, I'm going with the &quot;unironic Lawful Good heroic saint&quot; depiction of Saulot from early 2e. He foresaw the end and realized he needed to let the Tremere rise to power for both Kindred and Kine to prevent Gehenna or at the very least be able to survive it.<br /> <br /> As for the Baali? If I were to include them in a chronicle, I'm gonna go with the &quot;Always Chaotic Evil&quot; Chick Tract-tier strawman Satanist versions of the Baali from First Edition, but I'm gonna totally rewrite their backstory. Saulot had no hand in their creation but instead it was the work of Sutekh. A failed experiment of Set gone wrong.<br /> <br /> The first Baali was the Methuselah Shaitan, his name a corruption of Set-Han, in fact, Shaitan tried to usurp Set alongside his siblings Moloch and Nergal. They went renegade and consorted with demons to try and gain more power and overthrow Set. Yet the Baali are far more base and crude than the Setites in their quest to spread total corruption.<br /> <br /> But that was long ago and the Baali no longer care for Set nor his Followers while the elder Setites still hold a deep-seated hatred of the Baali, though most Setite neonates and ancilla who are aware believe the Baali to be extinct. Even a few Elders believe the Baali to be a mere historical footnote.<br /> <br /> But the most ancient of Setite elders still know and still remember. They know the Baali are still around and that Set has not forgiven them for their treachery.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T12:05:23-07:00","id":1520228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed?p=1520143#post1520143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think if you want you can even forcefully say that he faked his own death or what woke up wasn't the Ravnos in fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can easily go with that. The Master of Illusion dying like that seems...bizarre. Anticlimactic even. Sometimes death of the author is the best way to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T13:32:21-07:00","id":1520232,"title":"","content":"Ever since BJD came out I\u2019ve run with the option from the end where Enoch says he and the Antediluvians aren\u2019t nearly as powerful as they lead people to believe.<br /> <br /> In game this means that even Caine started out as about a 4 BP/2 dot discipline cap thinblood vampire, but over millennia his blood thickened all the way up to my 50 BP/9 dot cap.<br /> <br /> Gehennas occur every time the blood thickens enough for a new generation of vampires to hit the power ceiling\u2026 which simultaneously frees these ancients from old dominations by their sires and grants them the power to take on the other ancients. This leads to powers struggles and violence and the final deaths of some of the weaker \u201cold bloods\u201d and \u201cnew bloods\u201d as a new balance of power is established among the max strength vampires.<br /> <br /> In my game it is the 5th Generation that is rising into the 50 BP/9 dot category, threatening the old power bases, by the time it\u2019s done every Generation will be effectively a step up (i.e. 14th Gens will be able to access their full blood pool and learn the fifth dot in their disciplines; 8th Gens will start to be able to raise their traits to 6 and their blood gets 33% more potent).<br /> <br /> Which means Antediluvians in my setting are just 4th Gens with a LOT of extra XP compared to the 4th Gen Methuselahs\u2026 which means they can certainly die and many have likely been replaced over the millennia.<br /> <br /> Biblical Cain may not even be the 1st Generation, just the first known generation\u2026 and some other vampire was the true \u201cBlood Caine\u201d (in the sense of Mitochondrial Eve; the vampires\u2019 common ancestor. We\u2019ll never know their true name and they might have even met final death millennia before Biblical Cain was even born\u2026 so we may as well call this hypothetical creature Caine).<br /> <br /> So, basically, not only can an Antediluvian die, unknown numbers of them certainly already have\u2026 but the ever thickening blood means there will always be others to rise and replace them. Over millennia history will forget they ever weren\u2019t a part of the oldest generations.<br /> <br /> In my home game notes Biblical Caine was actually of the 21st Generation as measured from Blood Caine. Lilith was a vampire of the 20th Generation when she embraced him after killing nearly all of the 19th and prior generations.<br /> <br /> Biblical Caine believed himself the first vampire (believing Lilith to be just a blood witch) and so Cainites number their generations from him, but a few of the older survivors of Lilith\u2019s purge (such as the sleepers worshipped by the Baali) do confuse things in the historical record (some of Antediluvians rumored to be Lilith\u2019s children are, in fact, of the same Generation as Biblical Caine, but are counted as Caine\u2019s childer because while they have the same potential, Caine has more experience and so is perceived as being of an older generation).<br /> <br /> Hell, because of the cap, Shaitan/Nergal is probably the most singularly powerful vampire in my setting as he\u2019s achieved max vampiric power level with demonic investments layered atop that.<br /> <br /> TL;DR\u2026 setting a power cap plus thickening blood lets me play rather fast and loose with Antediluvians and their mortality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T08:30:16-07:00","id":1520388,"title":"","content":"If I were going to actually stat the Antediluvians, then this would be how I'd go about it. Bear in mind this would be for my own V20 headcanon that basically is summed up as &quot;The entirety of Revised and V5 never happened&quot;<br /> <br /> Attributes: 13/11/9, Abilities: 19/12/7<br /> Willpower: 10<br /> Path Rating: Humanity 0 (with a few noted exclusions listed below)<br /> Disciplines: All in-clan Disciplines at 10, plus Potence, Celerity, and Fortitude at 5 (if out-of-clan), Auspex at 6 (if out of clan), and Thaumaturgy at 5 (Tremere has Thaumaturgy 10, obviously)<br /> <br /> When it comes to the &quot;Humanity 0&quot;, that doesn't necessarily mean a Wight. For some Antediluvians, it can mean they are just criminally overpowered Wights but others hew closer to the 1e definition of Humanity 0 (basically an irredeemably corrupt yet functional villain)<br /> <br /> Now, for certain specific Antediluvians, they have Path ratings that are very different. <br /> <br /> Sutekh is at Path of Typhon 10<br /> <br /> Lord Tremere is at Humanity 1, whenever his soul is in control of his body<br /> <br /> Augustus Giovanni would either be a &quot;1e Humanity 0&quot; Kindred or he'd be on Road of Death 10, I'm honestly not sure which one fits better.<br /> <br /> Saulot is at Road of Heaven 10 and his soul has achieved Golconda since I prefer the early 2e &quot;unironic Lawful Good saint&quot; version of Saulot and the Salubri.<br /> <br /> Cappadocius would be at Road of Death 10 as well<br /> <br /> Ennoia would be Road of the Beast 10","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T11:32:45-07:00","id":1520537,"title":"","content":"I prefer not not give the 3rd generation any stats in general other then what their humanity or path rating is set at. Call me old school in that regard in wanting the most ancient kindred not having defined stats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T11:58:10-07:00","id":1520540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed?p=1520388#post1520388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were going to actually stat the Antediluvians, then this would be how I'd go about it. Bear in mind this would be for my own V20 headcanon that basically is summed up as &quot;The entirety of Revised and V5 never happened&quot;<br /> <br /> Attributes: 13/11/9, Abilities: 19/12/7<br /> Willpower: 10<br /> Path Rating: Humanity 0 (with a few noted exclusions listed below)<br /> Disciplines: All in-clan Disciplines at 10, plus Potence, Celerity, and Fortitude at 5 (if out-of-clan), Auspex at 6 (if out of clan), and Thaumaturgy at 5 (Tremere has Thaumaturgy 10, obviously)<br /> <br /> When it comes to the &quot;Humanity 0&quot;, that doesn't necessarily mean a Wight. For some Antediluvians, it can mean they are just criminally overpowered Wights but others hew closer to the 1e definition of Humanity 0 (basically an irredeemably corrupt yet functional villain)<br /> <br /> Now, for certain specific Antediluvians, they have Path ratings that are very different.<br /> <br /> Sutekh is at Path of Typhon 10<br /> <br /> Lord Tremere is at Humanity 1, whenever his soul is in control of his body<br /> <br /> Augustus Giovanni would either be a &quot;1e Humanity 0&quot; Kindred or he'd be on Road of Death 10, I'm honestly not sure which one fits better.<br /> <br /> Saulot is at Road of Heaven 10 and his soul has achieved Golconda since I prefer the early 2e &quot;unironic Lawful Good saint&quot; version of Saulot and the Salubri.<br /> <br /> Cappadocius would be at Road of Death 10 as well<br /> <br /> Ennoia would be Road of the Beast 10</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are interested, I <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383952-v20-antediluvians-peach#post1383952\">made a post </a>with the known and suspected stats of 3 antediluvians and some of their minions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T13:57:20-07:00","id":1520546,"title":"","content":"The 3rd generation is largely absent from our games and the closet is members of the 4th-6th generations as the eldest and still being somewhat active. Other wise it\u2019s members of 7th-11th generation being the most visible mover and shakers of kindred society. Though we did keep the subplot of Ravnos being almost extinct for reasons unknown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T17:24:30-07:00","id":1520560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed?p=1520540#post1520540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you are interested, I <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383952-v20-antediluvians-peach#post1383952\">made a post </a>with the known and suspected stats of 3 antediluvians and some of their minions.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I might write up some of my own stats for each of the specific Antediluvians as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T18:20:51-07:00","id":1520564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed?p=1520560#post1520560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, I might write up some of my own stats for each of the specific Antediluvians as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please share them when you are finished. I would be very interested in comparing with the Gehenna book and the others sources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T13:21:01-07:00","id":1520702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed?p=1520546#post1520546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 3rd generation is largely absent from our games and the closet is members of the 4th-6th generations as the eldest and still being somewhat active. Other wise it\u2019s members of 7th-11th generation being the most visible mover and shakers of kindred society. Though we did keep the subplot of Ravnos being almost extinct for reasons unknown.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I\u2019ve mentioned my notes about the ancients previously, I\u2019m pretty much in the same boat. My games all take place in a city where nearly every vampire 8th Gen or younger.<br /> <br /> The two that aren\u2019t are a reclusive low-humanity 7th Gen Ventrue (who runs things via his dominated Childe who is the official Prince of the city because of all the complications involving his dietary requirement of feeding on slaves) and a 6th Gen Baali passing himself off as an 8th Gen Assamite goodwill ambassador while the Clan is negotiating entry into the Camarilla (but has secretly been using his powers to sow dissension and exacerbate strife between the city\u2019s factions in a effort to sink the city into sin for his masters).<br /> <br /> The power difference between a very experienced 8th-10th Gen and a starting 10th-13th Gen is more than enough for the PCs to be underdogs without ever needing the elder disciplines and such.<br /> <br /> Conversely, I\u2019ve had both Shaitan and Tremere serve as major antagonists in my Mage campaign at various points; the former involving the discovery of an ancient tome that Shaitan sought, the latter in a heavily Order of Hermes based game where Tremere was trying to use the PCs as part of a gambit to restore himself to 3rd Gen status (this was long before BJD came out) after having transferred himself into Goratrix\u2019s 4th Gen body.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T14:29:45-07:00","id":1520705,"title":"","content":"Here's just a handful of stat sheets I made for the various Antediluvians. I don't have the Gehenna book with me anymore, so they aren't going to be compatible with anything in there. I'll probably make some more posts until I get all the Antediluvians stated up.<br /> <br /> Also, if you see Necromancy 10 or Thaumaturgy 10, assume that means all Paths and all Rituals are known to their absolute fullest extent on top of any plot device powers.<br /> <br /> Also, Clan Bushi do exist in my games as a rare Japanese bloodline believed to be tied to the Salubri and the Ventrue, so that's why Saulot, Tremere, and Veddharta all have the Kai Discipline. <br /> <br /> I'm going to start off with Saulot and Tremere, though I'm not going to even bother with the &quot;White Worm&quot; aspect of Tremere.<br /> <br /> Now, with other Antediluvians such as Tzimisce, Lasombra, and Malkav, I may try to stat out their non-humanoid forms such as the Cathedral of Flesh or the Malkavian Madness Network.<br /> <br /> <b>Saulot </b>(pre-diablerization) - AKA The Salubri Antediluvian<br /> <br /> Physical: Strength 7, Dexterity 7, Stamina 7<br /> Social: Charisma 8, Manipulation 9, Appearance 5<br /> Mental: Perception 10, Intelligence 9, Wits 8<br /> <br /> Path: Road of Heaven 10<br /> Willpower: 10<br /> Conscience: 10<br /> Self-Control: 10<br /> Courage: 10<br /> <br /> Disciplines: Auspex 10, Fortitude 10, Obeah 10, Valeren 10, Bardo 9, Obfuscate 7, Dominate 5, Presence 8, Animalism 7, Temporis 9, Kai 5, Potence 5, Celerity 5<br /> <br /> Abilities: Medicine 10, Empathy 9, Occult 9, Subterfuge 5, Alertness 9, Athletics 6, Awareness 10, Law 4, Melee 7, Survival 6, Stealth 5, Brawl 3, Expression 6, Performance 2, Etiquette 6, Science 3, Technology 1 <br /> <br /> Health Levels: 9 (OK, OK, -1, -1, -1, -2, -2, -3, -5)<br /> <br /> Notes: Has successfully achieved Golconda and would've been able to achieve Rebirth had he not been Third Generation (a headcanon of mine is that Antediluvians are so close to Caine that they cannot achieve Rebirth at all even if they reach Golconda. 4th Gen and lower can defeat the Curse of Caine but it's easier the further away you are from Caine in your generation. The only 4th Gen Methuselah who ever successfully achieved Rebirth was Osiris, who founded the Children of Osiris)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lord Tremere </b>- AKA The Tremere Antediluvian<br /> <br /> Physical: Strength 5, Dexterity 7, Stamina 5<br /> Social: Charisma 9, Manipulation 9, Appearance 6<br /> Mental: Perception 9, Intelligence 10, Wits 9<br /> <br /> Path: Humanity 1<br /> Willpower: 10<br /> Conscience: 1<br /> Self-Control: 7<br /> Courage: 10<br /> <br /> Disciplines: Auspex 10, Dominate 10, Thaumaturgy 10, Potence 5, Celerity 5, Fortitude 5, Valeren 1, Vicissitude 2, Animalism 6, Presence 8, Obfuscate 7, Kai 3, Chimestry 5, Kineticism 5, <br /> <br /> Abilities: Occult 10, Awareness 10, Leadership 10, Science 9, Subterfuge 9, Academics 9, Alertness 8, Empathy 8, Expression 8, Intimidation 7, Law 7, Crafts 7, Stealth 6, Etiquette 6, Technology 6, Larceny 6, Survival 5, Computer 5, Medicine 5, Politics 5, Melee 4, Finance 3, Brawl 3, Athletics 2, Streetwise 1, Firearms 1, Drive 1,<br /> <br /> Health Levels: 10 (Same as Saulot but with an extra OK level)<br /> <br /> Notes: Lord Tremere is one of only two Antediluvians who have been awake after 1500 alongside fellow usurper Augustus Giovanni. Though he often spends long amounts of time in torpor, his soul is often traveling the Astral Plane to divine more arcane knowledge nd lore and he has occasionally been semi-awakened from time to time over the centuries. Thus he has been able to learn about elements of the modern world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T14:40:23-07:00","id":1520706,"title":"","content":"I think the Goratrix must be more like 3 humanity, if you allow my opinion, in 1 you are nearly a animal.<br /> <br /> Also, with the level 10 disciplines being something far beyond the normal, Plot Device, I believe that the best thing is for him to only have 9 in dominion, level 10 would be more of a Ventrue thing. Among other details, I think presence is also too high and it would make more sense for him to know about other disciplines like Necromancy and Oblivion, another thing I didn't understand is why skills like empathy, computers and technology are high.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27832,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","user":"Psicose","date":". 08-15-2023, 06:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T14:48:34-07:00","id":1520709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed?p=1520706#post1520706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Goratrix must be more like 3 humanity, if you allow my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>For my headcanon, Lord Tremere's soul usually inhabits his own body (or is at least controlling the body), though Saulot occasionally will take over to decipher more info about the modern world but he is unable to awaken in Tremere's body just yet. Saulot's soul mostly is in a limbo of sorts, hanging around the Umbra/Astral Plane and he rarely holds Tremere's body for very long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T15:09:35-07:00","id":1520714,"title":"","content":"Those old stats bring memories of trying to figure out how someone with attribute ratings of 6 and up could be played. When I think of someone with a charisma of 4 or 5 I'm thinking of a George Clooney or Athletics 4 or 5 as a Lebron James, Serena Williams, Kevin Durrant, or a Gordon Hayward levels when he isn't injured and can't play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T15:39:57-07:00","id":1520719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed?p=1520709#post1520709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For my headcanon, Lord Tremere's soul usually inhabits his own body (or is at least controlling the body), though Saulot occasionally will take over to decipher more info about the modern world but he is unable to awaken in Tremere's body just yet. Saulot's soul mostly is in a limbo of sorts, hanging around the Umbra/Astral Plane and he rarely holds Tremere's body for very long.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, but that didn't explain why he have 1 of humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T19:48:53-07:00","id":1520734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed?p=1520719#post1520719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, but that didn't explain why he have 1 of humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>No but it did explain why he wasn't in Goratrix's body.<br /> <br /> Tremere's got Humanity 1 mainly due to his diablerie of Saulot and his crusade against the Salubri. He's nowhere near as evil as someone like Set or Tzimisce, but he's still pretty fucking bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T06:47:48-07:00","id":1520765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed?p=1520734#post1520734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No but it did explain why he wasn't in Goratrix's body.<br /> <br /> Tremere's got Humanity 1 mainly due to his diablerie of Saulot and his crusade against the Salubri. He's nowhere near as evil as someone like Set or Tzimisce, but he's still pretty fucking bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I had Tremere turn up in my Mage campaign, I always portrayed him as somewhere between a high 3 to low 4 Humanity (since nothing in Mage directly interacts with it I wasn\u2019t particularly concerned about a specific number).<br /> <br /> The heart of my decision was just that Tremere is thousands of years younger than even most Methuselahs and is younger than even some Mage NPCs\u2026 so he defaults to the same general Humanity tier as most active elder vampires (and the entire point of his involvement was his being active).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T10:05:09-07:00","id":1520774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed?p=1520702#post1520702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I\u2019ve mentioned my notes about the ancients previously, I\u2019m pretty much in the same boat. My games all take place in a city where nearly every vampire 8th Gen or younger.<br /> <br /> The two that aren\u2019t are a reclusive low-humanity 7th Gen Ventrue (who runs things via his dominated Childe who is the official Prince of the city because of all the complications involving his dietary requirement of feeding on slaves) and a 6th Gen Baali passing himself off as an 8th Gen Assamite goodwill ambassador while the Clan is negotiating entry into the Camarilla (but has secretly been using his powers to sow dissension and exacerbate strife between the city\u2019s factions in a effort to sink the city into sin for his masters).<br /> <br /> The power difference between a very experienced 8th-10th Gen and a starting 10th-13th Gen is more than enough for the PCs to be underdogs without ever needing the elder disciplines and such.<br /> <br /> Conversely, I\u2019ve had both Shaitan and Tremere serve as major antagonists in my Mage campaign at various points; the former involving the discovery of an ancient tome that Shaitan sought, the latter in a heavily Order of Hermes based game where Tremere was trying to use the PCs as part of a gambit to restore himself to 3rd Gen status (this was long before BJD came out) after having transferred himself into Goratrix\u2019s 4th Gen body.</div> </div> </div> </div>How old is your city that choose to set your game in? The closet city to me is barely 150 years old and we used it on how likely the eldest members of the Kindred would likely be and what generations they would be. We had a hard time picturing a member of the 4th-6th generation being there and the same with members of the 7th generation and decided that since we were playing Anarchs that the main players would be of the 9th-11th generation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T05:34:50-07:00","id":1520801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed?p=1520774#post1520774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How old is your city that choose to set your game in? The closet city to me is barely 150 years old and we used it on how likely the eldest members of the Kindred would likely be and what generations they would be. We had a hard time picturing a member of the 4th-6th generation being there and the same with members of the 7th generation and decided that since we were playing Anarchs that the main players would be of the 9th-11th generation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I decided to completely rewrite Boston and make it my own; the old version was lame and leveraged none of the city\u2019s history and unique traits (a Malk prince who thinks he\u2019s King Arthur? Really?) and this was before the new material came out (which I chose to ignore because the campaign had been going for years by that point).<br /> <br /> As such, I decided that the oldest vampire in Boston was in life a trader in opium, rum and slaves born in England in the late 17th Century, then relocated to Salem and eventually Boston (basically an expy of John Cabot, founder of one of the Boston\u2019s Brahmin first families)\u2026 he was embraced into the 7th Generation of Ventrue c. 1760. All the Ventrue in the city are his descendants.<br /> <br /> He, the Brujah who exert influence over Harvard, and the Tremere and their influence over the Free Masons are the big players in the city. But he is also very reclusive due to his dietary restrictions and crumbling humanity making it harder for him to handle the day to day which is now handled by his Childe, another Boston Brahmin (and former member of the Dashwood\u2019s Hellfire Club) and is the direct ancestor of extant Ventrue recognized in Boston (who, per Cabot\u2019s established rules of Embracing for his line must come from one of the Boston Brahmin families).<br /> <br /> I decided on 7th Gen because North America is still the New World to European vampires and so 7th Gen represents the last bit of the Old World bleeding over into the new with a very reclusive Elder and the rest being 8th+ Gen vampires embraced since Boston\u2019s founding.<br /> <br /> The 6th Gen Baali (very much in the mold of Shaitan/Nergal\u2026 Path of Evil Revelations and all) was just because I wanted someone even stronger than the Ventrue Elder with enough elder power to cause problems for the entire city (all while presenting a friendly and helpful face to the Court of Boston).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T15:22:02-07:00","id":1520837,"title":"","content":"Your right Chris23601 in changing VTM's take on Boston with what you told me about the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T03:56:51-07:00","id":1536974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511173-antediluvian-destroyed?p=1511185#post1511185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, you don't usually use things like the <i>Week of Nightmares</i> and other side effects for the clan as a whole?<br /> To be honest I never liked the idea behind the <i>Week of Nightmares</i> very much, I remember at the time there were people jokingly saying that it was &quot;the way Justin Achillis found to basically 'delete' the clan he said he didn't like&quot; lol<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Actually, it's just as possible as the ST wants it to be. My question is more aimed at STs in general as it's harder to find PCs who would ever be able to have a hand in such things, unless we're running a Gehenna scenario. Just as a sidenote, there are Mages and Cainites who are able to create destructive forces similar in power to a nuclear explosion, so it's not that hard to imagine a scenario where one NPC is able to successfully attack and destroy an Antediluvian. As I said before, it all depends on what the ST wants for his story.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I see, but then it was more of a Gehenna scenario, right? I've run one such scenario about 15 years ago. Likewise, I was more curious regarding the destruction of a single Antediluvian in an ongoing chronicle and its effects than with an &quot;apocalyptic scenario&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The specific Antediluvian (fictional) that you're referencing had level 10 Fortitude, over 10,000 years to develop multiple unknown variations of &quot;Plot Device&quot; Fortitude, and level 10 Chimerstry, in which he could have literally &quot;Noped&quot; out of the whole situation, and left doppelganger that was literally real to die.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I agree, it was just a way to kill a Clan that the developers didn't like. I wish that had been the Tzimisce, which make absolutely no sense, and are way overpowered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}